    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u00b7 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the create-owner flow while keeping the flat `address` backward-compatible. Each change went where that concern already lives:\n\n**Contract \u2014 `openapi.yml` (`OwnerFields` schema)**\n- Added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` properties (drives the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` getters/setters and the response DTO).\n- Made `address` optional (removed from `required`), since a request may now supply the structured form instead. Required is now `firstName, lastName, city, telephone`.\n\n**Persistence \u2014 `Owner` entity + all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres)**\n- New `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns and accessors, so the structured fields round-trip through save\u2192reload and MapStruct maps them by name automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\n**Address logic \u2014 `OwnerAddresses`** (kept as pure string helpers, single responsibility)\n- Existing `normalize(...)` unchanged.\n- Added `compose(line1, line2)` \u2014 the composition rule: `line1`, plus a single space and `line2` only when `line2` is present.\n- Added `isPresent(line)` for the non-blank test shared by the normalizer and validator.\n\n**Orchestration \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** (POST pipeline, runs first)\n- Structured form wins: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalize `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and compose the flat `address` from them; otherwise normalize the flat `address` alone (unchanged legacy path).\n\n**Validation \u2014 `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields`**\n- Address is satisfied by a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** the flat `address`; only both-blank reports `address` missing. City/telephone/names unchanged.\n\n**Update path \u2014 `ApplyOwner`** (PUT) now carries `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` through alongside `address`, so an owner update preserves the structured fields.\n\nBecause the flat `address` is composed from the structured fields whenever they're present, every existing consumer that reads `getAddress()` transparently sees the structured-derived value.",
